   "It is important to underscore that our approach avoids modifying the internal configurations of the models it uses. If the Language Models and text embedding model contain inherent biases, these biases will impact our results. Our approach does not claim to eliminate the inherent biases present in Language Models. Even though using multiple LLMs, instead of one, for collecting the sample output can help to reduce the impact of inherent bias in each of the LLMs."
   This paragraph discusses a key limitation: the inherent biases in the models. It also mentions a potential mitigation (using multiple LLMs). This is a core scientific contribution because it identifies a critical limitation and a possible solution (which is a form of analysis and problem formulation). It is important for understanding the constraints of the method.

 Paragraph 3:
   "Our approach heavily depends on the effective- ness of the embedding vectors produced by (Su et al., 2023) and their ability to capture the subtle semantic biases present in phrases. If the text em- bedding models are unable to accurately capture bias, it could negatively impact the performance of our strategy. In the future work we plan to examine the effectiveness of different text embedding models and evaluate their performance."
   This paragraph identifies another critical limitation: the dependency on a specific embedding model (Su et al., 2023) and the ability to capture semantic biases. It also mentions future work. This is a core limitation that directly affects the method's performance and is a key point for the scientific contribution.

